<!--
  A seal hauled out on the sand, head up, facing left.

  Drawn resting rather than swimming on purpose: this icon marks a sighting, and
  the sighting that matters most in this app is an animal on the beach rather
  than one in the water. Sea lions share it - see SightingSpecies, which explains
  why the app offers both names but only one drawing.

  The head runs continuously into the body with no drawn neck. An earlier version
  gave it a round head on a narrow neck and the silhouette read as a duck; a seal
  out of water is one tapering mass from snout to flippers, and that taper is
  what identifies it.
-->
